  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1: Frost/freeze conditions are probable Monday night \ninto early Tuesday morning over the western & central Alleghenies\n\nThe coldest air of the early Autumn season will push southeast \ninto Central PA early this week with frost/freeze conditions \nexpected Monday night into early Tuesday morning over much of\nthe western and central Alleghenies (northwest of I81). We\nissued a freeze watch for 4 counties in the NW Alleghenies\nleaning a bit colder vs. NBM/MOS blend. Placement of sfc high\nbecomes somewhat less favorable for frost/freeze Tuesday night. \n\n-------------------------------------------------------------\n \nKEY MESSAGE 2: Extended stretch of dry and seasonable Fall \nweather this week\n\nLow clouds entrenched on the eastside of the Allegheny Front \nwith embedded areas of light rain, drizzle and fog will \ngradually improve tonight into Monday as the mean low level flow\nshifts from the east/southeast to the west/northwest behind a\nsecondary cold front. The colder WNW flow could bring a couple \nof rain showers downwind of Lake Erie tonight into early Monday.\n\nOtherwise, we continue to have high confidence in a prolonged \nstretch of dry and seasonable Fall wx this week (Mon-Fri) as a \nlarge area of Canadian high pressure dominates the pattern.",
